! F.frr — Stub AS, customer of A
!
! F has a single upstream connection to provider A (10.1.1.2).
!
! As a stub, F:
!   - Announces ONLY its own prefix to A (no transit offered to anyone).
!     The base BGP config's 'network' statement already ensures this — only
!     F's loopback (10.255.6.1/32) is originated into BGP.
!   - Accepts all routes from A, giving F full global reachability through A.
!
! Money logic:
!   F pays A for transit. In return, A provides F with a full routing table
!   and propagates F's prefix to the rest of the internet. F has no incentive
!   to offer transit to others (it has no other neighbors to transit between).

route-map FROM-PROVIDER permit 10
 set local-preference 100
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  neighbor 10.1.1.2 route-map FROM-PROVIDER in
 exit-address-family
!
